{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, sorry the VPN is giving you trouble in Lisbon. Your account, VPN access and Duo sign-in all look fine, and the VPN worked from Lisbon earlier this week. We can't see any recent failed attempts reaching our VPN server, so the hotel Wi-Fi is probably stopping the connection before it gets to us. Please try these steps in order: 1) Open a browser and go to any public website. If the hotel's Wi-Fi sign-in or terms page appears, accept it and confirm normal websites load. 2) Close the VPN app completely and reopen it, then connect again. 3) If it still fails, restart your laptop and try once more. 4) When the Duo request appears, open Duo Mobile on your phone and pull down to refresh if the push doesn't show up. If none of this works, reply with the exact error message the VPN shows, and say whether normal websites load without VPN. Separately, your laptop is very low on disk space (about 9 GB free). Clearing out old downloads or large files when you have a minute will help it run smoothly. Good luck with the presentation!",
  "internal_note": "KB-013 checks: account active, failed_login_count 0, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true. Duo enrolled (push, Leo's phone). Sign-in logs: VPN worked from Lisbon PT (198.51.100.66) on Oct 7, 8 and 9 at about 09:05 local time, all with Duo push. No failed_password or mfa_denied entries, and no failed VPN attempts logged, so the current attempts are probably not reaching the server. Travel pattern is consistent (NY, then Lisbon client visit, matches the ticket), and there are no hosting-network sign-ins, so nothing suspicious. Most likely cause is the hotel captive portal or a client problem, so I sent KB-013 fix steps 2-4 (captive portal, restart client and laptop, Duo refresh). Escalation criteria not met: attempts aren't reaching the server and this is a single user. If the user says internet works, the portal is accepted and it still fails, escalate to Tier 2 under KB-013. Also noticed: BL-LT-0106 low disk warning (3.5% free, 9 GB). Mentioned it to the user, see KB-017 if it causes problems.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-016"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
